      "front": "For an ideal resistor, write the three equivalent expressions for power dissipation in terms of voltage $V$, current $I$, and resistance $R$, and state the SI unit of power.",
      "back": "The power dissipated by an ideal resistor is $P = VI = I^2R = V^2/R$. The SI unit of power is the watt, where $1\\ \\text{W} = 1\\ \\text{V}\\cdot\\text{A}$."
