      "front": "In a simple mark-recapture survey, $M$ animals are initially marked, $C$ animals are caught later, and $R$ of that later catch are marked. What is the estimated population size $N$ when $M=40$, $C=50$, and $R=10$?",
      "back": "Use the simple mark-recapture estimate $N = \\frac{M C}{R}$. Substituting the values gives $N = \\frac{40 \\times 50}{10} = 200$ animals."
